        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): add default 30s timeout to read and write WebClients",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`resolveSlackWebClientOptions` and `resolveSlackWriteClientOptions` do not set a default request timeout. All read and write Slack API calls (`chat.postMessage`, `users.info`, `conversations.list`, `reactions.add`, etc.) could hang indefinitely if the Slack API is slow or unresponsive. The lookup client already had a 30s timeout (`SLACK_LOOKUP_TIMEOUT_MS`), but the regular read/write clients did not.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extensions/slack/src/client-options.ts`: Add `SLACK_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000` and apply it via `??=` to both `resolveSlackWebClientOptions` and `resolveSlackWriteClientOptions`\n- Explicit `timeout: 0` (upload completion) is preserved by `??=`\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Real Slack API timing (token redacted):**\n```\nHost: LIN-66D8BD4EA2C\nDate: 2026-07-14\n\nGET /api/conversations.list: 200 in 0.57s\nGET /api/users.info:         200 in 0.62s\nGET /api/emoji.list:         200 in 0.70s\nGET /api/conversations.history: 200 in 0.61s\nGET /api/reactions.get:      200 in 0.66s\n```\n\n**Unit tests (2 new + 34 existing):**\n- applies default 30s timeout to read client when no timeout specified ✅\n- applies default 30s timeout to write client when no timeout specified ✅\n- preserves explicit timeout override for read client (60_000) ✅\n- preserves explicit timeout override for write client (timeout: 0) ✅\n\n**Lint + type check:** no errors\n\n**Coverage:**\nAll WebClient creation paths: `createSlackWebClient`, `getSlackWriteClient`, `createSlackWriteClient`\nAffected files: `send.ts` (3 sites), `actions.ts`, `channel-type.ts`, `probe.ts`, `resolve-users.ts`, `resolve-channels.ts`\n\n**Diff:**\n```diff\n+const SLACK_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000;\n\n export function resolveSlackWebClientOptions(...) {\n   ...\n   resolved.retryConfig ??= SLACK_DEFAULT_RETRY_OPTIONS;\n+  resolved.timeout ??= SLACK_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS;\n }\n\n export function resolveSlackWriteClientOptions(...) {\n   ...\n   resolved.retryConfig ??= SLACK_WRITE_RETRY_OPTIONS;\n+  resolved.timeout ??= SLACK_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS;\n }\n```\n\n## Review\n- Manually reviewed and verified\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
        "branch": "fix/slack-send-timeout",
